# Stablecoin Notes

## Why Stablecoins Matter

Stablecoins provide a reliable digital asset for payments, transfers, and financial applications. Unlike volatile cryptocurrencies, their value is designed to remain stable, making them more practical for everyday use.

---

## Stablecoins in ARC

One of ARC's main ideas is building a blockchain around stablecoins instead of treating them as an optional feature. Native USDC plays an important role in helping developers create faster and more efficient financial applications.

---

## Benefits

- Predictable value
- Efficient onchain payments
- Better user experience
- Lower settlement friction
- Easier integration for developers

---

## Personal Learning Notes

While reading the ARC documentation, it became clear that stablecoins are more than just a payment asset. They serve as the foundation for applications such as remittances, digital commerce, treasury management, and programmable finance.

This stablecoin-first approach is one of the biggest differences between ARC and many traditional blockchain ecosystems.

